<title>SWITZERLAND: Geneva April inflation falls to 0.2 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Geneva April inflation falls to 0.2 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1996-04-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumer prices in Geneva, Switzerland's third biggest city, fell 0.1 percent in April from the month before for a year-on-year inflation rate of 0.2 percent, the city statistics office said.</p>
<p>				    Apr 1997	Mar 1997	Apr 1996</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index change   -0.1 pct	-0.1 pct	+0.1 pct</p>
<p> Yr/yr inflation		+0.2 pct	+0.5 pct	+1.1 pct</p>
<p> Index (May 1993 = 100)	  104.3	   104.5	   104.1</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
</text>
